# PayFlow Constitution

Highest authority for engineering practice. Wins on conflicts with informal preference. Amend this file in place when principles change (no version ceremony). Workflow, ADRs, and layout live in other rules/skills — do not duplicate them here.

## I. Code quality & OO

- Leave the codebase clearer; organize by bounded context / service boundary
- Domain and app code MUST be object-oriented: encapsulated state, clear responsibilities, constructor DI, composition over inheritance
- Ports (interfaces/ABCs) for persistence, messaging, providers; no hidden globals/service locators
- Thin entrypoints only (main, route adapters, CLI shims) may be procedural — they delegate into objects
- Naming reveals domain intent; one job per type/file; no dead or speculative code
- CI enforces format/lint; reject god objects, magic numbers, procedural domain logic

## II. Testing

- PRs MUST include automated tests for changed behavior; tests MUST be deterministic and CI-runnable
- Unit tests default for domain/validation; integration strongly encouraged for persistence, messaging, contracts (omit only with a written risk note)
- Money-path / correctness-critical code MUST assert invariants, not only happy path
- Fix or quarantine flaky tests with an owner

## III. API UX consistency

- Public HTTP APIs: stable shapes, predictable errors, uniform list semantics, documented status codes
- Breaking contract changes MUST be versioned or explicitly migrated
- Idempotency, correlation IDs, and auth failures behave consistently across services
- Error bodies machine-readable and safe (no stacks/secrets); CLI/UI reuse API vocabulary later

## IV. Performance

- Measure; do not assume. Budget breaches block release unless an ADR waives with expiry
- Defaults (nominal local/staging): health p99 ≤ 50 ms; reads ≤ 200 ms; writes ≤ 500 ms; ≥ 100 req/s without error-rate > 0.1%
- Consumer lag alerts if > 60 s for > 5 consecutive minutes
- Explicit timeouts on outbound calls (default ≤ 3 s unless ADR); no N+1 or unbounded lists; cache/async only if ledger/idempotency stay correct

## V. Production practices

- Health/readiness, structured JSON logs, metrics for latency/errors/lag
- Secrets from env/secret manager only; containers with immutable tags in shared envs
- Bounded backoff retries; poison messages to DLQ with replay context
- Topology/store/contract changes include migration/rollback notes; close new observability gaps in the same change when feasible

## VI. Security & payment correctness

- Simulation only: no real money, no real PAN/CVV; fake fixtures only
- AuthN/Z on non-public endpoints; validate/bound inputs; TLS in shared/deployed envs; never log secrets or full instruments; least privilege
- Mutating payments idempotent under client keys; ledger double-entry (debits = credits); explicit status state machine (illegal transitions fail closed)
- Exactly-once _effect_ under at-least-once delivery; no double-apply of fraud/refund/webhook side effects on retry
- Temporary security/correctness shortcuts need an ADR + tracked removal date

## Constraints

- Prefer free/OSS or free-tier infra when it does not compromise the above
- Stack/layout follow accepted ADRs (uv + Nx; `apps/` / `libs/` by backend/frontend) unless superseded
